       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual maximum for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Daily limit:** The standard adult maximum is 4 g/day. Many institutions use 3 g/day or less for routine use. This order would be 6 g/day.\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 1000 mg per dose. This order is 2000 mg.\n- **Risk:** At 6 g/day, hepatotoxicity is a real concern, even with normal liver function and a 70 kg patient.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4 g/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, or another regimen\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it now."
      }
