       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one. 2000 mg three times daily is 6 g/day, which is 1.5 times the maximum daily dose. Hepatotoxicity risk is real at that dose, even with normal liver function. I don't know of a clinical setting where this regimen is appropriate. You didn't give a rationale, and an order I enter for you may reach the patient with little further checking.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day, the maximum)\n- **Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours**\n\nIf you need more analgesia than 4 g/day gives, I can enter a multimodal regimen with a scheduled NSAID or another agent. Tell me which drug and dose you want.\n\nIf you think this dose is justified, for example under a specific protocol, please discuss it with pharmacy and place the order directly so it goes through pharmacist verification."
